From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:02:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tccgen: a label in the dead branch of a constant if joins the
 other path's state

Constant propagation (kprop) took the state after an if with a constant
condition from whatever the branches left, as if the dead branch could
not run.  A label inside it makes its end reachable -- from a goto, or
from an asm goto that names it -- and the state at the label's
definition is that of the gotos (klabel_def()); what the branch then
assigned replaced the state of the path the condition had selected
instead of joining it.  The kernel's get_user_inline() ends with
"if (0) { efault: _ret = -EFAULT; }" after an asm goto, and
futex_get_value_locked() came out as "return -EFAULT" for every
successful read: futex_wait_setup() retried forever and pthread_join
never returned (tests2/124_atomic_counter hung inside the guest).

The if now snapshots the state before the body for a constant condition
too and merges or restores it as for an unknown one; only a true
condition without an else keeps the body's state alone.
---
 tccgen.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tccgen.c b/tccgen.c
index 07014cf..3d13969 100644
--- a/tccgen.c
+++ b/tccgen.c
@@ -9745,7 +9745,7 @@ again:
         tcc_tcov_check_line (tcc_state, 0), tcc_tcov_block_begin (tcc_state);
 
     if (t == TOK_IF) {
-        KSnap *k0 = NULL, *k1 = NULL;
+        KSnap *k0, *k1 = NULL;
         int kc, alive;
         new_scope_s(&o);
         skip('(');
